msgid "**7.2** Data is always stored off-chain. Off-chain metadata storage currently uses the IPFS storage operated by the portal provider; IPFS is the current default and, at this time, the only storage backend implemented and available in the Data Portal, and it cannot yet be changed via the frontend. UdL has no control over this Data. Ensuring the confidentiality, integrity and availability of the Data is in the sole responsibility of the Customer. The information describing and locating the Data (including any access credentials provided for such storage) forms part of the Service Offering metadata and is encrypted by the Ocean Node. Only metadata relating to Data is stored on-chain. To provide for the functionality of the Data Portal UdL indexes such on-chain metadata in a database operated as part of its Ocean Node. **Metadata and Service Offerings must not contain Personal Data**."
